# Golden: Phase-7 node 9210 (Option-2 generated lead) -- "samba" style, VarD
# peak section, a |C|F| two-bar change. Locks samba's generated kLeadMotif
# (the new TrackRole::kLead pattern in samba.hpp's kDP, no other section):
# seed=1302, length=6, center_degree=7 (a full octave above tonic), vel=78,
# gate=kGateStaccato, idiom_role=kPerc (onset candidates drawn from
# kPercRich's own guiro/cowbell even-16th mask, NOT the drums), gm_program=72
# (Piccolo -- the owner's anti-sameness call vs bossa's Flute, see
# docs/proposals/phase7-9210-motif-generate-option2-leads.md section 4.1).
# Two full bars of VarD exercise BOTH halves of the call-and-response repeat
# policy (motif.hpp's apply_repeat): bar 1 (repeat=0, over C) plays the
# generated phrase verbatim -- the "statement" -- and bar 2 (repeat=1, over F)
# applies the seed's own kDiatonicTranspose with a repeat-keyed amount -- the
# "answer". Routes drums/bass/chord1 following arranger_band.acmd's own
# convention, plus `style route lead synth:7` -- WITHOUT this route the new
# kLead content never appears in the golden at all (the gap this fixture
# closes). Any accidental change to samba's kLeadMotif or to kPercRich's onset
# mask moves these notes/ticks and fails this test.
key C major
port open out virt as synth
chord out synth:4
style load samba
style route drums synth:10
style route bass synth:2
style route chord1 synth:3
style route lead synth:7
style section varD
seq new verse
seq add C 1bar
seq add F 1bar
seq loop on
seq play
transport start
advance 7680
quit
